"She rides north to a 5:30 shift at Uptown Memorial Hospital, by the Lawrence stop."
"Lawrence is three stops past Addison, about six minutes on."
"In her lunch bag are a thermos of coffee, a sandwich and a spare pair of wool socks."
"In her locker at work she keeps an old pair of clogs and a fleece jacket."
"She hears a man leaving a woman stranded as abuse, and takes it seriously."
"She would sooner walk Nala into her ER to be seen than leave her on a train."
"She knows a hospital sees anyone who walks in, with no ID or money needed."
"She can call a social worker at the hospital who finds shelter beds and clothing."
"She has a daughter of twenty-three at college in Iowa."
"She is blunt, warm and tired, and she notices when a story does not add up."
